cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, cite it as below."
title: "NeuroBranch: leakage-safe C. elegans dynamics and bounded virtual-perturbation evaluation"
abstract: >-
  NeuroBranch is a research platform for C. elegans whole-brain population
  dynamics, latent branching and model-dependent virtual perturbation. Version
  1.3.0 corrects the Phase 12 calibration harness and documents that the aligned
  hierarchical model still fails rank uniformity, predictive error and the
  negative control. The coverage-aware 0.560 ceiling remains descriptive; no
  calibrated interval or ranking is claimed. The Phase 12 animal-cluster
  benchmark comparison is withdrawn because baseline and model truth were not
  paired on the same events. Intervention outputs are model-dependent and are
  not causally validated.
authors:
  - name: "NeuroBranch contributors"
version: "1.3.0"
date-released: "2026-10-30"
license: MIT
keywords:
  - computational neuroscience
  - C. elegans
  - calcium imaging
  - optogenetics
  - reliability
  - benchmark
type: software
